      "en": [
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "I know I have sinned, but I ask, please, Hashem, do not punish me \"out of anger\" but rather with love, in a way that Your punishments will help me see my mistakes and be a catalyst to correct them! At times I feel so weighed down with troubles, and with a feeling that I have missed opportunities and not lived up to my potential! But I am confident that You will accept my tefillah, give me opportunities to improve, and rid me of my difficulties, so that I can grow and serve You to my fullest potential—which is why You put me here on earth!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "You are the guardian of Yisrael; do not let Yisrael perish—in the merit that we say daily שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "You are the guardian of the one and only (אֶחָד) unique nation;"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 13
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "do not let that one and only (אֶחָד) unique nation perish—in the merit that we say daily that Hashem is אֶחָד!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "שׁוֹמֵר גּוֹי קָדוֹשׁ—You are the guardian of the separate and elevated (קָדוֹשׁ) nation; do not let that separate and elevated (קָדוֹשׁ) nation perish—in"
            }
          ],
          "anchorLine": 14
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "the merit that we (like the angels) declare daily קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ קָדוֹשׁ!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "מִתְרַצֶּה בְּרַחֲמִים—There is no power that can save us but You. Though we may not be worthy, deal with us with Your loving-kindness and chessed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "וַאֲנַחְנוּ לֹא נֵדַע—(To sum it all up:) Hashem, we do not know what else we can do, so we turn to You for Your kindness and help. We know we lack merit, but You know that we are material beings and thus have many struggles! Pardon us and give us another chance to prove ourselves, so that we may spread the knowledge of Your Presence to the whole world."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "spans": [
            {
              "text": "יִתְגַּדַּל וְיִתְקַדַּשׁ שְׁמֵהּ רַבָּא—(The chazzan proclaims our hope that) soon, in our lifetime, the entire world, which Hashem created precisely according to His Will, will recognize Hashem as the Source of all and will see the sanctity, perfection, and purpose of all He has done."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
